---
import CodeBlock from '../../../components/CodeBlock.astro'
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro'
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Kokoro speech"
  description="Use local Kokoro WASM narration in SuiteCut."
  section="kokoro"
>
  <p class="kicker">Field manual · 03</p>
  <h1>Kokoro speech</h1>
  <p>
    Kokoro 82M runs in a Node worker through <code>onnxruntime-web</code>. Inference stays local; no
    hosted model API or speech key is required.
  </p>

  <h2>Choose a voice</h2>
  <CodeBlock
    code={`suitecut.narrate('The final report is ready.', {
  provider: 'kokoro',
  voice: 'af_heart',
  speed: 1,
  caption: 'The final report is ready.',
})`}
  />
  <p>
    SuiteCut supports the 28 English Kokoro voices used by Spek. Useful starting points include
    <code>af_heart</code>, <code>af_bella</code>, <code>am_michael</code>, <code>bf_emma</code>, and
    <code>bm_george</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>Model cache</h2>
  <p>
    The first run downloads the quantized model, tokenizer, and chosen voice. Later runs reuse the
    cache. Set <code>SUITECUT_MODEL_CACHE</code> to choose another directory.
  </p>
  <div class="note">
    The first synthesis needs network access. Rendering after the model and voice are cached stays
    local.
  </div>

  <h2>Timeline behavior</h2>
  <p>
    Narrations are serialized. Each clip adds its measured duration and narration tail to the
    presentation timeline, so captions and speech do not overlap or slow the browser test.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
